<p>Very well done. Nice mixture of fucking creepy and extremely weird, which hits the notes of uncanny horror that I will always enjoy in works on this site. It captures a nice sense of essential wrong-ness that marks some of the better articles on the site. The stinger at the end, despite my issues, is a nice narrative flourish. Overall, a solid piece that I think was enabled by the contest parameters.</p>
<p>That said, I have a bit of a hard time with the twist at the end. It displays an amount of incredible stupidity on the part of the researcher involved, and while I know &quot;incompetent Foundation&quot; is a popular trope amongst some, it's never made any sense to me for quite a few reasons. Any number of things must have been running through the minds of the researchers working on this. I cannot imagine &quot;hey, I should invoke my own mother with this crazy teleporting head thing that doesn't obey the laws of god and man&quot; would ever be one of them.</p>
<p>Despite that, the storytelling skill involved overcomes my objections. Nice work.</p>

